#: SMD.md:1
msgid "Generating an unbinding trajectory"
msgstr "解離 Trajectory の生成"

#: SMD.md:3
msgid ""
"To generate a guess path for drug-target binding, we need the initial and "
"final reference states along with a tentative sampling of the process. In "
"most cases, the bound state of the drug-target complex is available either "
"though known experimental structures or docking predictions. However, "
"sampling the spontaneous drug-target dissociation with standard MD is "
"usually impractical due to timescale issues. To overcome this limitation, "
"one can leverage enhanced sampling methods. Herein, we resort to steered MD "
"(SMD), though other equally valid alternatives, such as adiabatic-bias MD, "
"are available."
msgstr ""
"薬物・標的結合の推定 Path には、初期・最終参照状態と、過程を試しに Sampling したものが必要です。結合状態は実験構造や Docking "
"予測から得られることが多い一方、標準 MD で自然解離を Sampling するのは時間スケール上困難です。Enhanced Sampling "
"を利用でき、ここでは Steered MD (SMD) を使います。Adiabatic-bias MD なども有効です。"

#: SMD.md:5
msgid ""
"As a test system to show the procedure for parameterizing a guess path, we "
"take the complex between the drug alprenolol and the $\\beta2$ adrenergic "
"receptor, which was more extensively studied in this work: "
"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.9b00450"
msgstr ""
"テスト系は Alprenolol と $\\beta2$ Adrenergic Receptor の複合体です。詳しくは "
"https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.jctc.9b00450 を参照してください。"

#: SMD.md:7
msgid ""
"Starting from the bound state of the complex, we pull along the distance "
"between the ligand and the binding site. In particular, we take as CV the "
"distance between the geometric centers of the low-fluctuating $\\alpha$ "
"carbons of the intra-membrane region of the receptor (ca) and the ligand's "
"heavy atoms (alp). We do this in a 10 ns SMD simulation, where we increase "
"the distance from its initial value to a target value of 30.0 Å and using a "
"force constant of 100 kcal/(mol * $Å^2$). For the receptor's atoms, we can "
"take the residue list from the published work. Fill in the following plumed "
"template to perform the SMD simulation:"
msgstr ""
"結合状態から Ligand と結合部位の距離に沿って引きます。CV は、Receptor の膜内領域の低揺らぎの $\\alpha$ Carbon "
"(ca) と Ligand の Heavy Atom (alp) の Geometric Center 間距離です。10 ns の SMD "
"で初期距離から30.0 Å まで増やし、Force Constant は100 kcal/(mol * $Å^2$) とします。Receptor "
"の残基一覧は論文から得られます。次の入力を完成させてください。"

#: SMD.md:30
msgid ""
"For the subsequent stages of the procedure, it is important to have a "
"trajectory that finely catches the system progression along the process. To "
"this end, we need to increase the saving frequency of MD snapshots. Setting "
"a dumping frequency value of 1 ps in the MD engine should be reasonable for "
"most applications."
msgstr ""
"後の手順には過程の進行を細かく捉える Trajectory が必要なため、MD Snapshot の保存頻度を上げます。多くの場合、MD エンジンで1 "
"ps 間隔とすれば妥当でしょう。"

#: SMD.md:32
msgid ""
"Once the simulation has completed, we can read the plumed output "
"*colvar_SMD.dat*, which stores different quantities recorded during the "
"simulation. For instance, we can inspect how strictly the system follows the"
" SMD restraint, and the work as a function of the distance CV:"
msgstr ""
"終了後、*colvar_SMD.dat* から記録された量を読みます。例えば、系が SMD Restraint にどれほど追従したか、距離 CV "
"に対する仕事を確認できます。"

#: SMD.md:34
msgid "![SMD](figures/smd.png \"Figure\")"
msgstr "![SMD](figures/smd.png \"Figure\")"

#: SMD.md:36
msgid ""
"As a final consideration, note that while the distance between ligand and "
"binding site increases, both the ligand, as well as the surrounding residues"
" from the target, are free to explore different configurations. For this "
"reason, it is good practice to perform a series of SMD simulations, and pick"
" the one where the work associated with the process is lowest. In first "
"approximation, this should better point to the minimum free energy path. "
"Additionally, the simulation parameters used herein were suitable to this "
"illustrative example and may need readjustements for application of "
"different systems. For instance, consider that different force constant "
"values or simulation time may be required. As an exercise, we can perform a "
"single replicate of SMD at increasing simulation times, e.g. 50 and 100 ns. "
"If we compare the work as a function of the distance CV in the three "
"simulations, we should obtain something like this:"
msgstr ""
"距離が増える間も、Ligand と周囲の標的残基はさまざまな Configuration を探索できます。そのため複数の SMD "
"を行い、仕事が最小のものを選ぶとよいでしょう。第一近似として、Minimum Free Energy Path "
"をよりよく示すと考えられます。ここでのパラメータは例示用で、別の系では Force Constant "
"や時間などの調整が必要です。演習として、50、100 ns など時間を延ばした SMD "
"を1本ずつ実行してください。3条件の仕事を距離に対して比較すると、次のようになります。"

#: SMD.md:39
msgid "![SMD](figures/smd_times.png \"Figure\")"
msgstr "![SMD](figures/smd_times.png \"Figure\")"

#: SMD.md:41
msgid ""
"As expected, allowing more time to the system for readjusting to more "
"favorable configurations as we pull the ligand outside the binding site "
"results in lower work."
msgstr "予想どおり、Ligand を引き出す際に有利な Configuration に再調整する時間を与えると、仕事が小さくなります。"
